{{template "base" .}}

{{define "title"}}{{.Data.Title}}{{end}}

{{define "attrs"}}class="container"{{end}}

{{define "body"}}
{{template "nav" .}}

<main id="main">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-center hero">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
        <h1 class="logo-header text-2xl">lend</h1>
        <div class="text-center text-lg">Remote commands, approved on your laptop</div>
        <a href="/getting-started.html" class="btn-link">GET STARTED</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="features">
      <div class="box">
        <h2 class="m-0 p-0 text-lg">
          Commands on your laptop
        </h2>
        <p>Keep tools such as <code>gh</code> and <code>op</code> local. Remote requests get the output and exit code back, under your <a href="/command-policy.html">command policy</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="box">
        <h2 class="m-0 p-0 text-lg">
          Your SSH agent, with approval
        </h2>
        <p>Choose which <a href="/ssh-keys.html">SSH keys</a> are visible and how they can sign. Each request is checked before it reaches your existing agent.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="box">
        <h2 class="m-0 p-0 text-lg">
          Review access locally
        </h2>
        <p>Use Touch ID on macOS or a local prompt on Linux. See the request, its reason, and its <a href="/approval.html">caller context</a> before you allow it.</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article>
      <pre><code># On your laptop
lend ssh --config ./policy.json -- agent-vm

# On the remote host
lend exec --reason "Inspect the pull request" -- \
  gh pr view 123 --repo example/project</code></pre>

      <div class="flex justify-center">
        <a href="/how-it-works.html" class="mt-4 btn-link">LEARN MORE</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <hr class="my-4" />

  {{template "footer" .}}
</main>
{{end}}
